><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20251008124101+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20251008124104+10'00'" name="0e07447f-526c-4788-9cd2-b5bc0946fd3e" page="9" coords="328.816000,457.278000,433.160000,457.278000,328.816000,443.869000,433.160000,443.869000,59.981100,444.295000,433.151000,444.295000,59.981100,430.887000,433.151000,430.887000,59.981100,431.257000,433.198000,431.257000,59.981100,417.848000,433.198000,417.848000,59.981100,418.273000,433.184000,418.273000,59.981100,404.865000,433.184000,404.865000,59.981100,405.291000,433.164000,405.291000,59.981100,391.883000,433.164000,391.883000,59.981100,392.309000,433.163000,392.309000,59.981100,378.901000,433.163000,378.901000,59.981100,379.269000,433.175000,379.269000,59.981100,365.861000,433.175000,365.861000,59.981100,366.287000,433.171000,366.287000,59.981100,352.879000,433.171000,352.879000,59.981100,353.305000,313.169000,353.305000,59.981100,339.896000,313.169000,339.896000" rect="59.562100,339.477000,433.617000,457.697000" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: This approach can help&#xD;scientists can gain additional insights to complement current notational analysis&#xD;approaches (Travassos et al., </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#00007F;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>2013</span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>). Second, there are significant implications for skill&#xD;acquisition. Fighters showed clear sensitivity to the affordances invited by their opponents’&#xD;action capabilities, suggesting that sampling an opponent in training is a key&#xD;constraint. While training with information-impoverished static targets (e.g. punching&#xD;bags, paddles and pads) is a common practice task of striking combat sports, these&#xD;findings suggest that such tasks may have some limitations and could compromise&#xD;transfer due to their lack of key informational constraints</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="9" rect="493.228000,365.278000,677.228000,457.278000"
/></highlight
